WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.192
<v Examiner>Three marks.

2
00:00:02.192 --> 00:00:07.404
<v Examiner>Identify two symptoms of anaphylaxis the nurse monitors for after a vaccination,

3
00:00:07.404 --> 00:00:09.879
<v Examiner>and describe the first-line treatment.

4
00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:12.001
Her formative two answers.

5
00:00:12.001 --> 00:00:15.729
One: noisy or difficult breathing, like stridor or wheeze,

6
00:00:15.729 --> 00:00:18.044
or swelling of the tongue or throat.

7
00:00:18.044 --> 00:00:22.094
Two: persistent dizziness or collapse, from low blood pressure.

8
00:00:22.094 --> 00:00:26.787
Breathing is the key one, she said: a rash or itch can be a mild allergy,

9
00:00:26.787 --> 00:00:30.901
but anaphylaxis is the extreme end, and it's what people die of.

10
00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.666
The treatment is adrenaline, intramuscular.

11
00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.687
In her scenario, nought point three milligrams,

12
00:00:36.687 --> 00:00:40.930
which is nought point three mils of the one in a thousand ampoule.

13
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.582
The vaccine words.

14
00:00:42.582 --> 00:00:48.058
Herd immunity: when most of a community is vaccinated, the infection can't spread,

15
00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:53.267
so the whole community is protected, including people who can't be vaccinated,

16
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.069
like babies.

17
00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:56.139
That's her formative three key.

18
00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:59.144
Vaccination is the act of giving the antigen.

19
00:00:59.144 --> 00:01:02.016
Immunisation is the memory the body builds.

20
00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:07.359
Active immunity is made by your own immune system: naturally after an infection,

21
00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:09.496
or artificially after a vaccine.

22
00:01:09.496 --> 00:01:15.239
Passive immunity is borrowed antibodies: naturally through the placenta or breastmilk.

23
00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:16.976
Live vaccines, like M M R,

24
00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:21.250
aren't given in pregnancy or to people who are immunosuppressed.

25
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.723
And common reactions, like a sore arm or mild fever,

26
00:01:24.723 --> 00:01:27.861
appear within a day and settle in one to three.

27
00:01:28.311 --> 00:01:33.363
Anaphylaxis: noisy or difficult breathing, stridor, wheeze, swollen tongue;

28
00:01:33.363 --> 00:01:34.844
dizziness or collapse.

29
00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:38.683
Treat with I M adrenaline, nought point three milligrams.

30
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:40.704
Mild allergy is rash and itch.

31
00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:45.014
Herd immunity: most people vaccinated, so everyone is protected.

32
00:01:45.014 --> 00:01:49.325
Live vaccines like M M R: not in pregnancy or immunosuppression.
